# SPA fallback for static hosting (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify).
#
# React Router handles /dashboard, /login, /reset-password and the rest in the
# browser, but the host looks for a FILE with that name first and there isn't one —
# only index.html. Without this rule, opening any deep link directly, or simply
# refreshing the page, returns 404. It works during `npm run dev` because Vite's dev
# server already does this fallback, so the problem only appears once deployed.
#
# Static assets are matched before this rule, so /assets/* still serves real files.
# Status 200 (not 301/302) so the URL the user sees is preserved and the router can
# read it — a redirect would rewrite the address bar and lose the route.
/*    /index.html   200
